Improved the textureLoader methods
All different texture methods are now renamed into a single `get_material()`. This will take a `Texture` as input. At the time of writing the `Texture` 'enum' contains the following items:
```js
const Textures = {
    grass: "grass.jpg",
    road_brick: "road_brick.jpg",
    road_gravel: "ground_gravel_crop.jpg",
    hedge_01: "hedge_01.jpg",
    hedge_02: "hedge_02.jpg",
}
```

## example
To create a new box and add a specific texture to it you can do the following:
```js
    const w = 10;
    const h = 1;
    const l = 75;

    const ob = new THREE.BoxGeometry(w, h, l);
    const object = new THREE.Mesh(ob, get_material(Textures.grass, w, h, l));
```

# House and Hedge classes
These have been updated to implement the new texture system.  Now you can create a new `House` and call `getMesh()` to get a Three.js object. After the fact you can still change the materials.

This PR fixes a bug where generated entity types were incorrect. It also improves dev error logging for schema errors.

For a given schema:
```graphql
type MyEntity @entity {
  id: ID!
  string: String
  nonNullString: String!
  stringList: [String]
  nonNullStringList: [String!]
  stringNonNullList: [String]!
  nonNullStringNonNullList: [String!]!
}
```

Before:
```ts
export type GobbledArtInstance = {
  id: string;
  string?: string;
  nonNullString: string;
  stringList?: string[];
  nonNullStringList: string[];
  stringNonNullList: string[];
  nonNullStringNonNullList: string[];
};
```


After:
```ts
export type MyEntityInstance = {
  id: string;
  string?: string;
  nonNullString: string;
  stringList?: (string | null)[];
  nonNullStringList?: string[];
  stringNonNullList: (string | null)[];
  nonNullStringNonNullList: string[];
};
```
